0_039_Chants_F_s.jpg","foto_urls":{"550X440":"https://images.schweizmobil.ch/image/ML_440_039_Chants_F_550x440.jpg","1800X1440":"https://images.schweizmobil.ch/image/ML_440_039_Chants_F_1800x1440.jpg","900X720":"https://images.schweizmobil.ch/image/ML_440_039_Chants_F_900x720.jpg","275X220":"https://images.schweizmobil.ch/image/ML_440_039_Chants_F_275x220.jpg"},"foto_master":"https://images.schweizmobil.ch/image-master/ML_440_039_Chants_F_M.jpg","foto_big":"https://images.schweizmobil.ch/image-big/ML_440_039_Chants_F_g.jpg","foto_standard":"https://images.schweizmobil.ch/image/ML_440_039_Chants_F_s.jpg","foto_small":"https://images.schweizmobil.ch/image-small/ML_440_039_Chants_F_k.jpg","foto_abstract":null,"logo":"https://images.schweizmobil.ch/image/ML_440_RF_140px.jpg","logo_svg":"https://images.schweizmobil.ch/image-svg/ML_440_Avrona_Bike.svg","x_coordinate":817316.891271743,"y_coordinate":185294.66175253148,"description":"On a plateau to the right of the Inn, there is the start of the bike tour. After Vulpera, once a world-famous health resort due to its mineral spring, the route leads on dirt roads past Chants to the transmission tower. From here, the view of the mighty castle Tarasp, the landmark of the Lower Engadine, is particularly beautiful. At this point, the bike route turns.\n\nWe take the forest road towards Avrona, ride past at the car park of the picturesque mountain lake Lai Nair. A detour is worthwhile: quiet and – as the name suggests – nearly black, it is located on an upland moor above Tarasp.\n\nOnce more, the last descent from Avrona down to Vulpera requires concentration and good riding skills: on a track, especially built for bikers, we enter the forest. This is immediately followed by a steep downhill. The snappy and fast single trail leads around trees, over roots and stones. With well-developed bends and turns, it spoils us all the way down to the starting point in Vulpera.","length":6,"length_asphalt":0,"length_unsurfaced":4,"length_sing